## Assumption Challenge
alternate vertices considered: runners, gaps, fixed circle sections,
section boundaries, wall-crossing events, residues, cover arcs,
individual survivor gates, mirror orbits, dead-cover labels, quotient
fibers, and proof obligations.
chosen carrier vertices: terminal exception packets in the union of
boundary-current failures and hard mirror-orbit rows.
preserved predicate: which legal terminal exit can discharge an LRC14
row after the universal E/branch gate producer has fired.
destroyed by scalarization: whether the row is hard-but-currented,
small-touch-but-not-hard, AP84 edge-only, or the unique random031 overlap.

