## Lemma Target
Finite audited form:
  The HYP-3472 currentless frontier and HYP-3475 hard-orbit frontier
  intersect only at random_covering_031.
  The six hard rows outside random031 already have a separating
  E/branch boundary current, so hard mirror debt need not be the
  terminal obstruction there.
  The six non-AP currentless rows outside random031 have no hard
  mirror orbit; their best touching gates have total adjacent-delta <= 3.
  The two AP84 currentless rows have projection edge cuts and are routed
  to the closed AP84 endpoint/corridor/color packet.
  Thus only random031 carries both defects, matching HYP-3455/HYP-3460.
  No existing HYP-3474 colored-gate quotient axis subset preserves this
  six-label terminal route partition; a later proof must carry the route
  sidecar R or prove a reconstruction theorem for it.

